{
  "$comment": "The wrinkle library — GitHub issue #159, GAMEPLAY_AND_NAVIGATION.md § 17. A day's twist is a row here rather than a literal in shift/events.ts, which is CLAUDE.md invariant 7 pointed at content. Every template's effect is expressed ONLY in fields the engine actually reads (arrivalRateMultiplier, directionalSplit, carsOutOfService, derate), because a template that named an effect nothing consumes would be a caption that lies about the picture under it — the defect shift/events.ts was written to prevent. Three of the six wrinkle kinds § 17 names are therefore NOT here and are recorded in `unexpressible` with the seam each one needs. The figures are DRAFTED, not measured: a wrinkle is game feel, and the ladder is the product owner's. See packages/viz/src/wrinkles/.",
  "version": 1,
  "unexpressible": [
    {
      "kind": "doors slowed on one car",
      "needs": "A per-car door-timing override on the run. `EventEffect` reaches cars only through `carsOutOfService` and `derate`, both of which remove a car rather than slow one, so a `doors-slowed` template would render a note no passenger experiences."
    },
    {
      "kind": "a sky lobby closed",
      "needs": "A service-zoning override on the run. Closing a transfer floor is a `BuildingConfig` change (service zoning), and `EventEffect` writes demand and car availability only. Collapsing it into a directional split would be a different day wearing the name."
    },
    {
      "kind": "a floor's occupancy spiked",
      "needs": "A per-floor population override on the run. Occupancy is building fabric; the nearest reachable lever is the whole-building directional mix, which moves every floor at once and so does not describe one floor spiking."
    }
  ],
